cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenDesigner or its research in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenDesigner: an open-source, AI-first design system builder and its research base"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bairwa
    given-names: Kunal
  - name: "OpenDesigner contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ckryptickunal/OpenDesigner"
url: "https://github.com/ckryptickunal/OpenDesigner"
abstract: >-
  OpenDesigner is a set of Agent Skills, knowledge files and a small engine that
  lets any capable AI model (Claude, ChatGPT, Codex and others) interview a person,
  recommend sourced defaults and generate a complete design system: DTCG design
  tokens, CSS and Tailwind exports, a DESIGN.md and a decision log. Its
  recommendations come from a cited research base of Decision Cards across color,
  typography, space, shape, motion, icons, brand, tokens, components, platforms,
  process, UX laws, device classes, visual principles, tooling and AI distribution,
  plus a teardown of 25 public design systems.
keywords:
  - design system
  - design tokens
  - DTCG
  - accessibility
  - WCAG
  - Agent Skills
  - Claude
  - ChatGPT
  - Codex
  - Figma
